  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "4Lmg2o206OTnjMnfGW38phIxf84=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:43:06.990Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`@powerhousedao/opentelemetry-instrumentation-reactor` inspects `ReactorModule` dependencies and subscribes to reactor event-bus events to register instruments covering the job queue, executor, read-model indexing and sync subsystems.\n\nIts scope is deliberately narrow: it **only creates OTel instruments on the global meter** and does **not** configure exporters or collector endpoints. The taxonomy states the same rule from the other side \u2014 the package itself reads **no environment variables**; all configuration belongs to the host's OTel bootstrap.\n\n```ts\nconst instrumentation = new ReactorInstrumentation(module); // module from ReactorBuilder\ninstrumentation.start();  // subscribe + register observable gauge callbacks\ninstrumentation.stop();   // remove all subscriptions, clear internal state\n```\n\nMetrics are recorded on the `@powerhousedao/reactor` meter via the global `@opentelemetry/api` `metrics.getMeter()`, so to see anything the application must configure a `MeterProvider` with an exporter in its entry point. The peer dependency is `@powerhousedao/reactor`.\n\nThe consequence for debugging: \"no reactor metrics\" has two very different causes \u2014 the instrumentation was never `start()`ed, or the host never wired a `MeterProvider`. The standard SDK variables a host typically sets are `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` (metrics export is disabled when unset) and `OTEL_METRIC_EXPORT_INTERVAL` (default 60000 ms).\n\n## Provenance\n- `packages/opentelemetry-instrumentation-reactor/README.md` \u2014 intro, scope note, Install and Usage\n- `packages/opentelemetry-instrumentation-reactor/docs/taxonomy.md` \u2014 Environment Variables\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:43:06.989Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:43:06.990Z"
    }
  },
